      "text": "The slope of the first line $y=2x+13$ is 2.\nFor two lines to be perpendicular, the product of their slopes must be -1.\nSo, the product of the slope of the first line and the slope of the second line must be -1.\nWe can set up the equation $2m=-(\\frac{-6}{a})$ and solve for $m$, the slope of the second line.\nCross multiplying, we get $a=3$.\nTherefore, the answer is $\\boxed{3}$.The answer is: 3",
